WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.153 --> 00:00:16.680
Anne been doing her lessons at home.

2
00:00:17.501 --> 00:00:24.625
One morning, however, Anne came into the kitchen with her schoolbooks and announced, "Marilla, I'm going back to

3
00:00:24.725 --> 00:00:30.348
school. I miss spending time with my best friend Diana, so I must return."

4
00:00:31.100 --> 00:00:32.721
Marilla hid her delight well.

5
00:00:32.742 --> 00:00:36.324
"I hope you'll behave yourself," was all she said.

6
00:00:37.766 --> 00:00:42.709
In January the Canadian premier toured Canada, including Prince Edward Island.

7
00:00:43.410 --> 00:00:49.295
Most of Avonlea supported the premier's politics, and many people, including Marilla and Mrs.

8
00:00:49.375 --> 00:00:52.157
Lynde, went to hear him speak in Charlottetown.

9
00:00:52.838 --> 00:00:55.500
They planned to return to Green Gables the next day.

10
00:00:56.264 --> 00:01:00.865
So Anne and Matthew had the cheerful, warm kitchen of Green Gables to themselves.

11
00:01:00.885 --> 00:01:05.167
"Matthew, did you ever study geometry?"

12
00:01:05.547 --> 00:01:06.127
asked Anne.

13
00:01:06.147 --> 00:01:09.328
"Well, no, I didn't," Matthew said.

14
00:01:09.348 --> 00:01:14.389
"I wish you had," Anne said, "because then you could sympathize.

15
00:01:15.069 --> 00:01:16.330
I'm terrible at it!"

16
00:01:17.050 --> 00:01:21.151
Suddenly the kitchen door flung open, and Diana Barry ran in.

17
00:01:21.171 --> 00:01:23.212
"What's the matter, Diana?"

18
00:01:23.592 --> 00:01:24.232
cried Anne.

19
00:01:24.844 --> 00:01:26.445
"Has your mother changed her mind?

20
00:01:26.986 --> 00:01:28.647
Can we be friends again?"

21
00:01:28.667 --> 00:01:31.328
"Oh, Anne, come quickly!"

22
00:01:31.749 --> 00:01:32.829
Diana urged her.

23
00:01:32.849 --> 00:01:37.733
"My little sister, Minnie May, is awfully sick—she's got croup.

24
00:01:38.513 --> 00:01:43.337
Father and Mother are in town at the premier's meeting and there's nobody to get the doctor.

25
00:01:43.997 --> 00:01:47.279
The baby-sitter doesn't know what to do, and I'm so scared."

26
00:01:47.900 --> 00:01:51.022
Matthew reached for his cap and went outside to get the horse.

27
00:01:51.042 --> 00:01:55.268
"Matthew will ride to Carmody for the doctor," said Anne.

28
00:01:55.968 --> 00:01:57.449
She quickly put on her coat.

29
00:01:57.469 --> 00:02:00.990
"Don't cry, Diana," she went on cheerfully.

30
00:02:01.010 --> 00:02:03.891
"I know exactly what to do for croup.

31
00:02:04.491 --> 00:02:11.933
Mrs. Hammond had twins three times, which gave me lots of experience because they all had croup regularly.

32
00:02:12.633 --> 00:02:15.414
I'll get the ipecac bottle in case you don't have any.

33
00:02:15.954 --> 00:02:16.434
Come on."

34
00:02:17.074 --> 00:02:21.896
The two girls hurried to the Barrys' house through the fields, for the snow was too deep to

35
00:02:21.936 --> 00:02:22.856
go the shorter way.

36
00:02:23.552 --> 00:02:29.916
Although Anne was sincerely worried about Minnie May, she was delighted to be spending time with Diana again

37
00:02:30.076 --> 00:02:30.977
outside of school.

38
00:02:31.778 --> 00:02:36.901
She thought it was truly wonderful to walk through the dark snowy night with her best friend.

39
00:02:37.601 --> 00:02:43.986
At the Barrys', Minnie May was feverish and restless, and her hoarse breathing rattled through the whole house.

40
00:02:44.746 --> 00:02:46.227
Anne promptly went to work.

41
00:02:47.308 --> 00:02:49.049
"Minnie May has croup all right.

42
00:02:49.610 --> 00:02:52.031
She's pretty bad, but I've seen worse.

43
00:02:52.592 --> 00:02:55.637
First we must have lots of hot water.

44
00:02:56.177 --> 00:02:59.559
Diana, fill up the kettle and put some wood in the stove.

45
00:03:00.319 --> 00:03:03.100
I'll undress Minnie May and give her some ipecac."

46
00:03:03.781 --> 00:03:08.443
The little girl did not take kindly to the ipecac, but Anne kept trying.

47
00:03:09.263 --> 00:03:15.166
She gave Minnie the ipecac many times during the long anxious night, but Minnie got worse.

48
00:03:16.586 --> 00:03:19.968
Anne thought Minnie was sicker than the Hammond twins ever were.

49
00:03:20.528 --> 00:03:24.909
It was difficult for Minnie to breathe, and it seemed like she could choke to death.

50
00:03:25.709 --> 00:03:29.190
Anne, losing hope, gave her the last drop of ipecac.

51
00:03:29.871 --> 00:03:34.432
In a few minutes, Minnie coughed up phlegm and began to get better right away.

52
00:03:35.112 --> 00:03:36.372
She soon fell asleep.

53
00:03:37.573 --> 00:03:40.954
It was three o'clock when Matthew finally arrived with the doctor.

54
00:03:40.974 --> 00:03:44.815
"I nearly gave up," Anne said to the doctor.

55
00:03:44.835 --> 00:03:49.096
"You can't imagine my relief when she finally seemed better."

56
00:03:49.800 --> 00:03:52.261
The doctor nodded and went to check on Minnie.

57
00:03:53.022 --> 00:03:56.864
Anne was exhausted from no sleep, and she went home with Matthew.

58
00:03:58.205 --> 00:03:59.706
In the morning Mr.

59
00:03:59.746 --> 00:04:00.186
and Mrs.

60
00:04:00.246 --> 00:04:01.226
Barry came home.

61
00:04:01.987 --> 00:04:05.009
The doctor, Diana, and Minnie were in the living room.

62
00:04:05.729 --> 00:04:07.030
The doctor told Mr.

63
00:04:07.070 --> 00:04:07.470
and Mrs.

64
00:04:07.530 --> 00:04:10.372
Barry, "That redheaded girl is a clever thing!

65
00:04:11.132 --> 00:04:13.233
I tell you, she saved that baby's life.

66
00:04:13.894 --> 00:04:16.615
For someone her age, she was smart and calm.

67
00:04:17.395 --> 00:04:18.056
It was wonderful.

68
00:04:18.676 --> 00:04:19.937
I've never seen anything like it."

69
00:04:21.098 --> 00:04:23.981
Anne didn't wake up until the evening of the next day.

70
00:04:24.841 --> 00:04:27.463
She went to the kitchen where Marilla sat knitting.

71
00:04:27.483 --> 00:04:31.907
"Anne," Marilla said, "Matthew told me about last night.

72
00:04:32.848 --> 00:04:35.110
It's very fortunate you knew what to do.

73
00:04:35.950 --> 00:04:40.774
I wouldn't have any idea myself, for I never saw a case of croup."

74
00:04:40.794 --> 00:04:44.257
"Mrs. Barry was here this afternoon, Anne," Marilla continued.

75
00:04:44.938 --> 00:04:47.280
"She wanted to see you, but you were sleeping.

76
00:04:48.012 --> 00:04:53.794
She says you saved Minnie May's life, and she's sorry she acted the way she did in the

77
00:04:53.855 --> 00:04:54.975
affair with the wine.

78
00:04:55.855 --> 00:04:59.537
She hopes you'll forgive her and be good friends with Diana again.

79
00:05:00.297 --> 00:05:02.378
You can go over there this evening if you like.

80
00:05:03.098 --> 00:05:05.379
Now, Anne, don't fly into the air!"

81
00:05:06.940 --> 00:05:10.521
The warning was needed because Anne instantly sprang to her feet.

82
00:05:10.541 --> 00:05:16.724
"Oh Marilla, can I go and see Diana right now without washing my dishes?

83
00:05:17.472 --> 00:05:18.753
I'll wash them when I come back.

84
00:05:19.434 --> 00:05:24.878
I can't do something so unromantic as dishwashing at this thrilling moment."

85
00:05:24.898 --> 00:05:30.123
"Yes, yes, run along," said Marilla indulgently, smiling.

86
00:05:31.684 --> 00:05:36.208
Anne ran through the orchard to the Barrys', not caring about the wind or cold.

87
00:05:36.908 --> 00:05:42.833
Mrs. Barry kissed her and cried, and said she was sorry and that she could never repay Anne.

88
00:05:43.574 --> 00:05:47.433
Anne was embarrassed but replied politely, "I forgive you, Mrs.

89
00:05:47.513 --> 00:05:52.475
Barry. I can tell you again that I did not mean to make Diana drunk."

90
00:05:53.435 --> 00:05:55.956
Diana and Anne had a lovely afternoon.

91
00:05:56.716 --> 00:06:00.178
Diana showed Anne a new crochet stitch her aunt had taught her.

92
00:06:00.978 --> 00:06:05.840
Then Diana gave Anne a beautiful card with a wreath of roses on it and a verse of

93
00:06:05.920 --> 00:06:11.982
poetry: "If you love me as I love you, nothing but death can part us two."

94
00:06:12.743 --> 00:06:19.140
At school Diana and Anne sat together again, and they were the happiest girls in Avonlea.
